; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; RESOLUTION-AFFECTING SETTINGS ARE GUARDED. infra/ci/npmrc-guard.mjs
; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
; Every line in this file applies to EVERY npm resolution with no command line
; to inspect: Dockerfile:31, the pre-merge gate, lockfile-maintenance.yml's
; deliberately-bare refresh steps, Dependabot's updater, and your laptop. The
; guard fails on any resolution-affecting key that is not on the record.
;
; ⭐ THE INSTALL FLAG AND THE LOCKFILE-GENERATION FLAG ARE NOT THE SAME
; DECISION, AND THIS FILE CANNOT TELL THEM APART. That is the whole reason
; `legacy-peer-deps` does not belong here. The deploy INSTALLS with it
; (Dockerfile:31) and must; nothing in this repo should GENERATE a lockfile
; with it. `.npmrc` applies to both, so one line would silently convert the
; second into the first.
;
; 🚨 `legacy-peer-deps=true` IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. droplinked-shopfront#693
; adopted it. Adopting it here was measured, on dev @ 21956bf, npm 10.9.3,
; node 22.18.0, and it is the wrong move:
;
;   INSTALL-time (the flag is a no-op — `npm ci` installs the lockfile, it
;   does not resolve; the flag only decides whether peers are VALIDATED):
;     npm ci                      890 packages, 3 unmet edges
;     npm ci --legacy-peer-deps   890 packages, 3 unmet edges   (same tree)
;
;   GENERATION-time, in place, from the committed lockfile (this IS what the
;   flag changes — measured in three isolated checkouts):
;     npm install --package-lock-only                      978 entries, byte-identical
;     npm install --package-lock-only --force              978 entries, byte-identical
;     npm install --package-lock-only --legacy-peer-deps   927 entries, 51 DROPPED
;
; The 51 are peer entries and their subtrees: @droplinked_inc/wallet-connection
; and @droplinked_inc/web3-kit (declared peers of the first-party runtime
; package @droplinked_inc/web3), webpack (peer of @sentry/webpack-plugin, and
; its 38-package closure), and fastestsmallesttextencoderdecoder (peer of
; @solana/codecs-strings). The peer-conflict ratchet reports 4 NEW unmet edges
; on that tree — and `next build`, `tsc --noEmit` and `npm test` all stay
; GREEN. A change to what ships that only one control in this repo can see.
;
; The condition #693 fixed does not exist here. There, Dependabot's
; `npm install --force --package-lock-only` diverged from the workflow's
; install and re-minted `"peer": true` nodes on every rebase. Here, in-place
; regeneration is byte-identical to what is committed, with and without
; --force. There is no divergence to fix; the line would create one.
;
; lockfile-maintenance.yml now asserts this after every refresh.

registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
save-exact=false
audit-level=high
